 "show": {
  "slug": "bigg-boss",
  "name": "Bigg Boss",
  "description": "India's biggest reality show: housemates, weekly nominations, evictions and the host's Weekend Ka Vaar.",
  "scope": "national",
  "country_code": "IN",
  "network": "Colors TV and JioHotstar",
  "overview": "Bigg Boss is India's version of the Big Brother format. A group of housemates, mostly people already known from television, film, music, sport or social media, move into one house for about three months. Cameras follow them all day, they have no contact with the outside world, and they take on weekly tasks that decide who gets privileges and who is at risk.\n\nEach week the housemates nominate each other, viewers vote, and someone leaves the house. The last one standing wins the trophy. That mix of living together, alliances that shift and public voting is why the show keeps starting arguments online long after an episode airs.\n\nThe Hindi version began on 3 November 2006 on SET, hosted by Arshad Warsi, and moved to Colors TV from the second season, which Shilpa Shetty hosted. Amitabh Bachchan hosted the third. Salman Khan has been the face of the show since the fourth season in 2010, and Sanjay Dutt co-hosted the fifth alongside him.\n\nSeason 19 began on 24 August 2025 and Gaurav Khanna won it, with Farrhana Bhatt as runner-up. Season 20, subtitled Tathas-two, premiered on 6 September 2026 on Colors TV and JioHotstar with 16 housemates, and is on air now. There are also Bigg Boss versions in Kannada, Telugu, Tamil, Malayalam, Marathi and Bengali, and a streaming spin-off, Bigg Boss OTT.",
